# L §5.5: "a line whose result read no option of an axis prints * for it"; "On a line, an axis prints * when,
# with the line's other options held, every option of it gives the line's result ... An axis printed * has no
# reading: entry."  For k = a the value doesn't depend on the axis; for k = b it does.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2016-03-01
  start 2015-11-01
  end 2016-10-31

source s "s"

axis mode
  low "a low reading"
  high "a high reading"

index ks = [a, b]
input v[m in mode]: int
input w: int

def r[k in ks]: int at reader
  rule base = w
  rule special beats base = v[mode] when k == b

version x
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2016-01-01
  v[low] = 1
  v[high] = 2
  w = 7

ask q1: r[k] for k in ks law 2016-03-01
=== expect
q1 (k = a) [mode = *]: 7
  law date 2016-03-01, cut 2016-03-01
q1 (k = b) [mode = low]: 1
  reading: mode = low
  law date 2016-03-01, cut 2016-03-01
q1 (k = b) [mode = high]: 2
  reading: mode = high
  law date 2016-03-01, cut 2016-03-01
